---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Navbar from "@/src/components/Navbar.astro";
import { caffeine_rush_banner } from "@/src/images";
import { People, Energy } from "@/src/images/icons";
import Row from "@/src/components/Row.astro";
import Link from "@/src/components/Link.astro";
import InlineLink from "@/src/components/InlineLink.astro";
import SectionTitle from "@/src/components/SectionTitle.astro";
import Layout from "@/src/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Buzzshot from "@/src/buzzshot.astro";
import CaffeineTitle from "@/src/components/CaffeineTitle.astro";
import Expander from "../components/Expander.astro";
import HelpEmail from "../components/HelpEmail.astro";
import Stopwatch from "@/src/images/icons/stopwatch.astro";
import DctMap from "../components/DCTMap.astro";
---

<Layout>
    <Navbar />
    <div class="bg-beige flex flex-col items-center pb-8 px-2 text-center">
        <Image
            src={caffeine_rush_banner}
            alt="Text Caffeine Rush in a playful font. A coffee cup spilling coffee"
            height={300}
            class="pt-8"
        />
    </div>
    <Row className="bg-brick border-none">
        <p class="text-center">
            <Link href="#bz-target" className="text-beige font-nougat text-3xl underline hover:no-underline hover:opacity-70">
                Book now &gt;
            </Link>
        </p>
    </Row>
    <Row className="bg-mikey border-none">
        <p class="text-center">
            <Link href="https://youtu.be/D4Xm4sC1ZAg?t=2410" className="underline font-bold text-beige">
                "The most fun I've had in, like, four, five months"
            </Link>
        </p>
        <p class="text-right text-beige">--- Quinns, Quinns Quest / People Make Games</p>
    </Row>

    <Row className="bg-beige-50 border-none text-brick-100">
        <CaffeineTitle>Baristas Wanted at Tony's Cafe</CaffeineTitle>
        <p class="text-md">...where the kitchen is heating up. Your job: serve all the customers before the time runs out. But you&apos;d better stay on your toes - who knows what curveballs you&apos;ll have to deal with next?</p>
    </Row>
    <Row className="bg-mikey border-none">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 justify-items-center gap-8 text-center text-beige">
            <div class="grid grid-rows-[4rem_auto] justify-items-center">
                <div class="flex h-16 items-center">
                    <Stopwatch className="w-14 h-14"/>
                </div>
                <span>60 minutes</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-rows-[4rem_auto] justify-items-center">
                <div class="flex h-16 items-center">
                    <People className="w-16 h-16"/>
                </div>
                <span>2-6 players</span>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-rows-[4rem_auto] justify-items-center">
                <div class="flex h-16 items-center">
                    <Energy className="w-16 h-16"/>
                </div>
                <span>Type: Frantic</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </Row>
    <Row className="bg-brick-100 border-none text-beige-50">
        <CaffeineTitle>Location: London Southbank</CaffeineTitle>
        <p>202 Blackfriars Road, SE1 8NJ</p>
        <p>Closest tubes: Southwark, Waterloo, Blackfriars</p>
    </Row>
    <DctMap/>
    <Row className="bg-beige-50 border-none text-brick-100">
        <CaffeineTitle>FAQs</CaffeineTitle>
        <Expander title="Is this an escape room?">
            <p>Kinda.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="What do you mean, 'kinda'? How can you be 'kinda' an escape room?">
            <p>It's like an escape room, in that it takes place in a room, with furniture, with a small team of your friends for 60 minutes.</p>
            <p>But instead of trying to solve all the puzzles as fast as you can, here your quest is to make as much coffee as you can to serve to customers. There might be some escape room style puzzles along the way though.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="I still don't get it. Explain it another way.">
            <p>It's like a video game, but in real life. There are some puzzles. Mostly you yell at your friends for not brewing the coffee fast enough. You might like it. You'll have to try it and find out.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="How many players can I bring?">
            <p>We think the game plays best with 4-6 people so we recommend those team sizes. You can play with 2-3 but it's a lot harder!</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="What's the age limit?">
            <p>Caffeine Rush is suitable for everyone. Children under 12 must be accompanied by an adult throughout. Children under 6 might find the game quite difficult but you are absolutely welcome to play as a mixed family group.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="Will it just be us in the room?">
            <p>Yes, you'll have the game to yourselves.</p>
            <p>Although you might have to report to your boss, Tony. Tony runs the cafe. He mostly prefers to stay out of the kitchen and tell you what to do.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="What level of physical activity is required?">
            <p>The game involves moving around a room carrying empty paper cups and interacting with machinery. There's time in between levels for a rest and a water break.</p>
            <p>If you like we can provide chairs to sit on during levels, though note that you probably want at least 1-2 team members to be standing and moving around during levels.</p>
            <p>If you want to know more about whether the game is a good fit for you, just drop us an email at <HelpEmail/>.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="Is the location step free?">
            <p>Unfortunately the building we are in is not step free. Our room is on the first floor up 21 fairly narrow steps.</p>
            <p>Once you have made it to the room, we can adjust the game so some players are entirely seated if you like. However, due to the nature of the game, at least 1-2 members of the team will need to be standing and moving around for most of the 60 minutes.</p>
            <p>If you want to know more about whether the game is a good fit for you, just drop us an email at <HelpEmail/>.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="What should I wear?">
            <p>The game takes place fully indoors and we have heating and air con.</p>
            <p>You might want to wear sensible shoes. The game is more fast-paced than most escape rooms so you might find yourself wanting to dash around quickly.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="Can I add/remove people from my booking?">
            <p>You can add people up to 6 when you arrive, just show up and we'll sort it out on the door.</p>
            <p>Unfortunately we don't allow refunds if someone on your team drops out.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="What's the deal on cancellations/refunds?">
            <p>If you want to cancel or change your booking, let us know on <HelpEmail/>. We'll see what we can do but can't promise anything.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="Any content warnings I should know about? [Mild spoilers]">
            <p>We have the option to include themes of alcohol in the game. When you book you'll be asked whether you'd prefer with or without alcohol. No actual alcohol is involved.</p>
            <p>If you'd like to know any other specific content advisory about the game, do get in touch: <HelpEmail/>.</p>
        </Expander>
        <Expander title="Did you use AI to make this?">
            <p>We used AI coding assistants to help build the software in the game and on this site. We use no AI in our art, writing, game design or music.</p>
        </Expander>

    </Row>
    <Buzzshot />
    <Row>
        <SectionTitle>Stay in the loop</SectionTitle>
        <p>
            Want exclusive discounts and updates on Tony's latest hijinks? Sign up for our <InlineLink
                href="https://buttondown.email/DreamcatPuzzles"
                >newsletter</InlineLink
            >!
        </p>
    </Row>
</Layout>
